5 cloves", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "5 cloves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "10 black peppercorns", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "black peppercorns", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "6 to 8 amarillo chilies or 4 dried guajillo chilies, rinsed, tops removed and seeded", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": 8.0, "unit": null, "item": "amarillo chilies or 4 dried guajillo chilies", "preparation": "rinsed, tops removed and seeded", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "4 basic tamales (see recipe)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "basic tamales (see recipe)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oil in a large, heavy skillet over medium heat. Add the garlic and onion and cook, stirring often, for 2 minutes. Stir in the tomatillos, cinnamon, oregano, cloves and peppercorns. Reduce the heat to low and simmer until the tomatillos are tender, about 20 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, place the chilies in a small bowl and cover with boiling water. Soak until very soft, 10 to 20 minutes. Place the tomatillo mixture in a food processor. Pulse to partly puree. Add the chilies, one at a time, tasting after each addition until the filling is as hot as you like it. Puree until smooth. Season to taste with salt. Follow directions for basic tamales."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 136.4, "protein_g": 3.4, "carbohydrates_g": 21.0, "fat_g": 6.1, "saturated_fat_g": 0.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 689.6, "fiber_g": 6.2, "sugar_g": 12.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_ser